  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the strongest setting so far (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), outperforming single-profile PCA and multiprofile transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet models are much weaker. This experiment tests whether replacing PCA with a learned nonlinear RNA encoder (scvi_n200) improves that best RNA-only setting, isolating the effect of RNA representation while keeping profile setting and aggregation fixed. It is the best next step because it exploits the most promising current direction with a controlled single-factor change, reduces uncertainty about RNA representation, and will inform whether learned RNA encoders should be used in later multimodal comparisons."
